# Making Sense of Genetics: Students' Knowledge Use during Problem Solving in a High School Genetics Class.

**Authors:** Finkel, Elizabeth A.

## Abstract
Examines ways in which students collaborate to construct, use, and revise conceptual and strategic knowledge as they solve complex genetics problems. Concludes that students used three types of knowledge during model revision: knowledge of genetics, knowledge of the process of model revision, and knowledge of their own problem-solving strategies (metacognitive knowledge). Contains 49 references. (JRH)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ522162

